{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Who says of his father and of his mother, 'I have not seen him.'</b> He speaks of the entire tribe, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 32:26–27): מי ליהוה אלי ויאספו אליו כל בני לוי, and he said to them: מלאו ידכם היום ליהוה כי איש בבנו ובאחיו — and not literally his son and his brother; so too here, לאחיו ולאמו and את אחיו ואת בניו — one should not interpret 'his father' literally, nor 'his brothers' literally from his father, nor 'his sons' literally, for they were full Levites, and in the tribe of Levi not one of them sinned at all, as it is written ויאספו אליו כל בני לוי. Rather, the sense of the verse is: לאביו — his mother's father, from Israel; ואת אמו — his mother's brother from Israel (i.e., his maternal uncle); ואת בניו — his daughter's son from Israel; and they were not Levites at all." "<b>For they observed Your word.</b> לא יהיה לך. <br><b>And Your covenant they kept.</b> This is the covenant of circumcision, for Israel did not circumcise their sons in the wilderness, but the tribe of Levi circumcised their sons. And although he speaks of the tribe in general, there is also alluded in it Samuel the prophet the Levite, and of him it is said האומר לאביו ולאמו לא ראיתיו, for when he was weaned he was in the house of HaShem, to be separated and set apart to serve the Holy One, blessed be He, and את בניו לא ידע — he did not know that he had begotten sons for the service of HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:02.526057938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}